  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health Information and Quality Improvement Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sri Lanka - RSSH - Ministry of Health of the Democratic Socialist  Republic of Sri Lanka - MOH.  This program has the following goals: Strengthening the health system which augments an effective, efficient, equitable, economical and quality health service while ensuring privacy and confidentiality of care recipients improving health outcomes.. The objectives of this program are: To provide quality and timely information for evidence-based decision making through the establishment of an ubiquitous, integrated, dynamic, cost-effective and sustainable health information system through the integration of vertical nationally scaled information systems through a digital HMIS platform..  To integrate TB Control activities into general healthcare system by establishing TB diagnostic and treatment services at base hospitals by 60% in 2021 and 100% by 2022..  Improvement of quality of care provided to the patients through improving targeted strategies in hospital quality management, improvement of quality of training of paramedical categories and laboratory investigations.</narrative>
  </description>
